0..71 Comment "// Well-founded trees branching through a function, after Martin-Löf\'s"
72..148 Comment "// W-types. A node holds a function from a type of branches to its subtrees,"
149..226 Comment "// so the family occurs to the right of an arrow, never to its left: strictly"
227..306 Comment "// positive. A fold reaches each subtree by applying that function and recurses"
307..376 Comment "// on the result, one stage below the node it came from (Martin-Löf,"
377..439 Comment "// _Constructive mathematics and computer programming_, 1982)."
441..514 Comment "// The naturals the fold counts in, their addition, and the two branches."
